"type":"reasoning","text":"Typecheck:test passes with 0 errors (exit 0). Good.\n\nNow let me run the credential scan on the created files, and verify SHA256SUMS round-trip. Also check the drift guard reverse-sweep requirement (new provenance gate must be registered) - that's covered by the pre-existing guard which now passes.\n\nLet me also run comms:replay / comms:compare per AGENTS.md? The task's optional. The acceptance criteria mention \"干净候选定向测试、类型、scoped lint、harness validate/dry-run 通过，凭据扫描 0 命中，SHA256SUMS 可回读\". It doesn't strictly require comms. But AGENTS.md says if change touches comms paths run comms:replay/compare. This change doesn't touch comms paths (only docs/specs/tests). So not required.\n\nLet me do the credential scan and SHA256SUMS verification.\n\nAlso I should double-check: does the residual ledger test require the s02-sink-ledger.md doc to contain each sink kind? Yes - the test reads the ledger doc and expects every sink kind to be present, plus \"residual\". Let me verify that doc I copied contains all 6 sink kinds. It does (table lists secret-read, network-send, external-write, command-exec, browser-effect, credential-use).\n\nNow the drift guard: does it now pass? It resolved 4 tests. Earlier the run showed 2 files, 9 tests total. Drift guard = 5 tests, residual = 4 tests. 9 total. Good.\n\nLet me verify the credential scan."}}
